Description:

In the WebDAV drive namespace (/dav/drive), collection names are now UTF-8
in the URL and are converted to and from the modified UTF-7 of the mailbox
name.  Previously, MKCOL of a name with a non-ASCII character or an
ampersand failed with 500 "Invalid mailbox name", and a client that sent
modified UTF-7 itself got UTF-7 back in PROPFIND hrefs and an empty
displayname.  Invalid UTF-8 is refused with 400.  A segment that is already
valid modified UTF-7 and contains an ampersand is still taken as it is.
CalDAV and CardDAV are not affected.


